BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 195.09 Td (While doing this search, we keep track of the last node visited at each level before as these are the predecessor) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 181.69 Td (nodes that\222ll point to our new node once inserted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 161.79 Td (Once we insert the element in Level 0, how do we decide if it should be inserted in other levels or no ?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 141.89 Td (The answer is that we flip a fair coin \(p = 1/2\) to decide if the node should be promoted one level up, or not.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 128.49 Td (HEADS promotes it one level higher; TAILS stops the promotion. So HEADS then TAILS means the node) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 115.09 Td (reaches Level 1. This coin-flip decides the height randomly, which is why skip lists are called probabilistic) Tj ET
